  "description": "Temporal is the open-source durable execution platform that lets developers write ordinary code and get fault-tolerant, long-running workflows without managing state, retries, or recovery themselves. Founded in 2019 by the creators of Uber's Cadence and AWS's Simple Workflow Service, it runs mission-critical systems at companies including OpenAI, Netflix, Snap, NVIDIA, and Stripe. Temporal Cloud processes billions of actions a month, and the company surpassed a $250M annualized revenue run rate in 2026 as durable execution became core infrastructure for long-running AI agents.",
